#: templates/report.html.j2:189
msgid ""
"This absolute median uses <b>all meals</b> in each slot, including "
"contaminated windows — as do the baseline-normalised curves below. The CR"
" table in Part 2 prefers contamination-free meals instead (at least 3 "
"clean, otherwise all), so its count (n) can differ; how much that "
"selection changes the picture is stated there."
msgstr ""
"This absolute median uses <b>all meals</b> in each slot, including "
"contaminated windows — as do the baseline-normalised curves below. The CR"
" table in Part 2 prefers contamination-free meals instead (at least 3 "
"clean, otherwise all), so its count (n) can differ; how much that "
"selection changes the picture is stated there."

#: templates/report.html.j2:192
msgid "Course relative to meal start (baseline-normalised)"
msgstr "Course relative to meal start (baseline-normalised)"

#: templates/report.html.j2:195
#, python-format
msgid ""
"Each meal is set to <b>0 at minute 0</b>, then the median is taken — the "
"typical\n"
"    <b>net course</b>. Its value at the end is the Δ%(w)s used later. "
"Ending negative → often below baseline\n"
"    (overdosing); staying high → underdosing. <b>All meals</b> of a slot "
"are shown here, like the\n"
"    absolute curve above: this is what happened, without any selection. n"
" can differ slightly when\n"
"    minute 0 has no CGM sample."
msgstr ""
"Each meal is set to <b>0 at minute 0</b>, then the median is taken — the "
"typical\n"
"    <b>net course</b>. Its value at the end is the Δ%(w)s used later. "
"Ending negative → often below baseline\n"
"    (overdosing); staying high → underdosing. <b>All meals</b> of a slot "
"are shown here, like the\n"
"    absolute curve above: this is what happened, without any selection. n"
" can differ slightly when\n"
"    minute 0 has no CGM sample."

#: templates/report.html.j2:203
msgid "Part 2 — assessment and how to read it"
msgstr "Part 2 — assessment and how to read it"

#: templates/report.html.j2:204
msgid "Everything from here rests on the method described in this part."
msgstr "Everything from here rests on the method described in this part."

#: templates/report.html.j2:207
msgid "How to read this report (CamAPS FX Auto Mode)"
msgstr "How to read this report (CamAPS FX Auto Mode)"

#: templates/report.html.j2:208
msgid ""
"• <b>Scope:</b> Built for CamAPS FX Auto Mode, where the algorithm mainly"
" corrects via\n"
"  <b>modulated basal</b> (not auto-bolus). Other AID systems need a "
"different signal."
msgstr ""
"• <b>Scope:</b> Built for CamAPS FX Auto Mode, where the algorithm mainly"
" corrects via\n"
"  <b>modulated basal</b> (not auto-bolus). Other AID systems need a "
"different signal."

#: templates/report.html.j2:210
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"• <b>Loop extra basal</b> in the post-meal window:\n"
"  <code>∫ (basal rate − fasting basal) dt</code>.\n"
"  Positive → extra Auto Mode activity after the meal. It can fit a too-"
"weak CR, but on real CamAPS it is not specific to that."
msgstr ""
"• <b>Loop extra basal</b> in the post-meal window:\n"
"  <code>∫ (basal rate − fasting basal) dt</code>.\n"
"  Positive → the loop is adding insulin (often a too-weak meal bolus/CR)."

#: templates/report.html.j2:213
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"• <b>Two ratios:</b>\n"
"  <code>CR (CHO/bolus)</code> = carbs ÷ meal bolus only (may include "
"correction insulin).\n"
"  <code>CR_eff</code> = CHO ÷ (bolus + loop extra basal) — effective "
"ratio <i>including</i> loop compensation.\n"
"  Neither is a programmed pump setting; both are derived from the export."
"\n"
"  If the loop already adds or cuts a lot of insulin with no meal, that "
"says nothing about the carb ratios. The less non-meal loop influence in "
"the window, the less CR_eff is shifted by that extra Auto Mode activity."
msgstr ""
"• <b>Two ratios:</b>\n"
"  <code>CR (CHO/bolus)</code> = carbs ÷ meal bolus only (may include "
"correction insulin).\n"
"  <code>CR_eff</code> = CHO ÷ (bolus + loop extra basal) — effective "
"ratio <i>including</i> loop compensation.\n"
"  Neither is a programmed pump setting; both are derived from the export."
"\n"
"  If the loop already adds or cuts a lot of insulin with no meal, that "
"says nothing about the carb ratios. If it runs quietly, the estimated "
"CR_eff moves a bit closer to a better ratio."

#: templates/report.html.j2:218
msgid ""
"• <b>Use:</b> Discussion material for the diabetes care team only — not a"
" dosing instruction."
msgstr ""
"• <b>Use:</b> Discussion material for the diabetes care team only — not a"
" dosing instruction."

